{"tool_name":"ddpcr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ddpcr","home":"https://daattali.com/shiny/ddpcr/","license":"MIT","summary":"ddpcr is a R package for droplet digital polymerase chain reaction visualization and analysis.","addition_date":"2018-10-31T22:20:21Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T17:46:05Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ddpcr","credit":[{"email":"jenny@stat.ubc.ca","name":"Jennifer Bryan","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6983-2759","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ddpcr/ddpcr.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"}]}],"name":"ddpcr","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.12688/f1000research.9022.1","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 Attali D et al.Droplet digital polymerase chain reaction (ddPCR) is a novel platform for exact quantification of DNA which holds great promise in clinical diagnostics. It is increasingly popular due to its digital nature, which provides more accurate quantification and higher sensitivity than traditional real-time PCR. However, clinical adoption has been slowed in part by the lack of software tools available for analyzing ddPCR data. Here, we present ddpcr - a new R package for ddPCR visualization and analysis. In addition, ddpcr includes a web application (powered by the Shiny R package) that allows users to analyze ddPCR data using an interactive graphical interface.","authors":[{"name":"Attali D."},{"name":"Bidshahri R."},{"name":"Bryan J."},{"name":"Haynes C."}],"citationCount":14,"date":"2016-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"F1000Research","title":"Ddpcr: An R package and web application for analysis of droplet digital PCR data [version 1; referees: 2 appro